A consumer position and its materialized state must agree. Acknowledge processing only after the promised processing completes.

> allowing a single stateful transaction to atomically update both the state and input offsets.

Source: [Q13](/lore/durability-bibliography#q13); [B5](/lore/durability-bibliography#b5-building-event-driven-microservices).

## Failure it prevents

Progress advances without its state, or state commits while replay still reapplies the event.

## Our Effect 4.0.0 reading

`SqlClient.withTransaction` covers its database boundary. `Stream.runForEach` expresses handling only. Broker acknowledgement and remote transactions need their own protocol.

Source: `packages/effect/src/sql/SqlClient.ts`, `packages/effect/src/Stream.ts`.

## How to check

Crash before and after state commit and acknowledgement. Redeliver and compare state with the expected checkpoint. This check is our proposal. The books do not prescribe it.

Continue with [Retry needs idempotent effects](/lore/retry-needs-idempotency), [Dead letters need a return path](/lore/dead-letters-need-a-return-path).

